@startuml ArtSearch_Corpus_Discovery_Loop
title ArtSearch Provenance-Preserving Corpus Discovery Loop

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1
autonumber

actor Operator
participant "Airflow or discovery CLI" as Runner
participant "Discovery oracles" as Oracles
participant "Bluesky AppView" as AppView
database "PostgreSQL discovery schema" as DiscoveryDB
participant "DiscoveryCoordinator" as Coordinator
participant "Bluesky hydrator" as Hydrator
participant "Existing SigLIP intake pipeline" as Intake
database "SQLite staging + local files" as SQLite
participant "CLIP/CSD downstream jobs" as HeavyML
database "Qdrant derived index" as Qdrant

Operator -> Runner : start bounded campaign
Runner -> DiscoveryDB : create campaign with config hash + budgets
Runner -> Oracles : manual/search/Starter Pack sources
Oracles -> AppView : ranked discovery reads
AppView --> Oracles : creator leads and provenance
Oracles --> Coordinator : DiscoverySuggestion stream

loop each unique DID within creator budget
  Coordinator -> Hydrator : fetch current profile
  Hydrator -> AppView : getProfile
  Coordinator -> DiscoveryDB : upsert creator + independent observation + edge evidence
  Coordinator -> Coordinator : profile safety policy
  alt blocked or excluded
    Coordinator -> DiscoveryDB : block state + exclusion
  else sample eligible or stale
    Coordinator -> DiscoveryDB : enqueue media task
  else fresh qualified score
    Coordinator -> DiscoveryDB : enqueue bounded graph expansion
  end
end

loop due frontier leases across current and interrupted campaigns
  Coordinator -> DiscoveryDB : claim with FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
  alt sample creator media
    Coordinator -> Hydrator : initial posts_with_media sample
    Hydrator -> AppView : paged author feed
    Coordinator -> Intake : classify and route sample
    Intake -> SQLite : decisions + accepted corpus rows
    Intake --> Coordinator : ordered ACCEPT/REVIEW/REJECT/ERROR evidence
    Coordinator -> DiscoveryDB : posts, stable media identity, model evidence
    alt preliminary creator qualifies
      Coordinator -> Hydrator : deeper bounded media sample
      Coordinator -> Intake : classify only unseen candidates
    end
    Coordinator -> DiscoveryDB : creator score components + explicit state
  else expand qualified creator
    Coordinator -> Oracles : outbound/suggested follows
  end
  Coordinator -> DiscoveryDB : complete, retry with backoff, or dead-letter task
end

Coordinator -> DiscoveryDB : finish campaign + coverage snapshot
SQLite -> HeavyML : accepted standardized artwork
HeavyML -> Qdrant : publish current CLIP subject + CSD style vectors

note over Oracles,DiscoveryDB
  A social/search observation is evidence, not an artist decision.
  Replays preserve one entity and multiple idempotent evidence records.
end note

note over DiscoveryDB,Qdrant
  PostgreSQL is canonical for discovery state.
  SQLite is worker staging; Qdrant is derived and rebuildable.
end note

@enduml
